# Pre-match presentation, shot for shot.
#
# The sequence PES stages between the loading screen and kickoff, transcribed
# from the reference broadcast in docs/PRESENTATION_SPEC.md section 1
# (video t~3185-3300). The kickoff is held until the whole thing has run.
#
# Format:  beat <name> <seconds> [camera=...] [overlay=...]
#
#   camera=walkout    low broadcast angle panning along the line of players,
#                     framed off the choreography itself
#   camera=lineup     static and head-on, holding the whole line in frame
#   camera=entrance   the imported PES entrance camerawork for this
#                     competition's family and this stadium, moved onto our pitch
#                     with the choreography it films - both are authored in the
#                     same coordinates, so they travel together. This is the one
#                     to use where a pack ships it: it has PES's own framing and
#                     focal lengths. The two above are computed from where the
#                     cast ended up, and are the fallback for a pack with no
#                     camerawork of its own.
#   camera=orbit      a slow authored sweep of the stands
#   camera=aerial     the high wide the live game is played on, held still
#   camera=hold       stay wherever the previous beat left the camera
#
#   overlay=formation_home / formation_away
#                     the TV-style lineup panel for that side
#                     (spec section 1.1)
#
# Competitions differ: drop <entrance_id>.timeline next to this file and the
# match picks it up automatically, or name one with "presentation_timeline".
# Unknown keys are ignored, so a file may carry more than this build reads.

beat stadium_card       12.0  camera=orbit

# The walk-on: ent_009's per-stadium packs start the squads outside the
# touchline and bring them in. The tunnel packs (ent_007 passage*) stage a
# three-metre corridor because PES plays them inside tunnel geometry - without
# that set they are a column of players walking up an empty pitch.
beat walk_on            22.0  camera=entrance shot=ent_009
beat line_up            16.0  camera=entrance shot=ent_009
beat anthems            20.0  camera=entrance shot=anth

beat wide_home           9.0  camera=aerial   overlay=formation_home
beat wide                4.0  camera=aerial
beat wide_away           9.0  camera=aerial   overlay=formation_away

beat team_picture       10.0  camera=entrance shot=circle_home

# Ends on the camera the match itself starts on, and stages nobody: the cast has
# left the field to the players by the time the whistle goes, so kickoff is a
# continuation rather than a cut.
beat to_kickoff          6.0  camera=aerial
